<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Surendra Sai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1809–1884</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Surendra Sai was a claimant to the throne of Sambalpur in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, who led a long armed revolt against British rule. Imprisoned at Hazaribagh from 1840, he was freed by mutineers in 1857 and fought a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war in the hills of Sambalpur until his surrender in 1862. Rearrested in 1864, he died in Asirgarh fort in 1884 and is honoured in Odisha as a freedom fighter.</p></div>
